{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1208627-on-a-wounded-throne-mk-iii","id":1208627,"title":"On a Wounded Throne, Mk.III","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-04-18T17:02:16-07:00","id":1208627,"title":"On a Wounded Throne, Mk.III","content":"Hello! It's Fitter Happier! I stopped writing for a couple years but now I'm back! I revamped a story I wrote when the very first hints on EX3 Lunars were released! Here it is!<br /> <br /> <b>***</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Once, this was a throne room, but that was wars and an age ago, when Alafia of the Burning Necklace did not hide herself at the edges of the world like a coward. That was before her halls were razed; her legions abased, tormented, and turned against her; before betrayal twisted every taste to bitter wine running between her teeth. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Alafia alighted on nightjar\u2019s talons, then stepped forward in her birth-face. Her eyes trailed up, stalking along the fractured mosaics that depicted her past triumphs. They showed her in her war-face, crushing a daimyo\u2019s crown in pincered fists. They showed her pouring out blood from a chalice. They showed her receiving powers and potentates from the tribes of chaos, and claiming their hearts as forfeit. All true, and now all forgotten. She walked on bare feet, mouth twisted with self-pitying sorrow</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">It was dark, but Alafia\u2019s eyes had the keenness of a cat\u2019s, glimmering with reflected starlight as she adjusted their shape with a thought. She let her hand part from the mosaic wall, and stepped forward into the atrium. At its center, on a raised dais, was a broken throne. Gingerly she walked across the shattered floor, and gingerly she lowered herself onto the stone seat. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">A thousand-thousand sorrows threatened to overwhelm her. A hundred years of bitter resignation beat them back. The pearl in her throat began to pulse and grow, skin distending with red light, but she swallowed it down, gulping rage and hatred like slabs of meat, her bitter feast, and the skin at her neck flattened and the light ebbed away. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">All lost! And only goblins left to sing her praises. She could hear them begin to scurry, still attuned to the protean Essence that shaped them, even after so many years. Alafia grimaced. She was well-practiced in the night-craft, the Lunar art of molding servants from the clay of chaos, but she could hardly stand to see her work debased by time and neglect. They once were clever creatures, but now their minds had gone, run like water from their grotesque heads.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">They were fit barely for raw material. But in her fallen state, could much better be said for their maker?</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Beneath the moon\u2019s hidden face, Alafia of the Burning Necklace began to brood.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">***</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">It was some time later, and Alafia\u2019s erstwhile creations had emerged in force. They stumbled like drunken toddlers, mewling and whistling and laughing and crying.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">\u201csing o muse,\u201d tittered a mindless goblin, hung by rope from a fallen rafter. Alafia flexed her arm, extruding her lissome sting, and silenced the creature.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">\u201cYou have fallen low, Prince of the Earth,\u201d came a rumbling, mocking voice. Lurching out of the shadow of a crumbled pillar, dragging a heavy tail, Inyonyi Yamanzi regarded Alafia with reptilian gazes. Nicitating membranes flickered across her black eyes. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Inyonyi\u2019s tastes always ran to the monstrous. Her massive crocodile-jaws hung open. Her four lion-taloned paws scuffed the ancient dust on the floor. She shook her head, scattering more dust from the reeking mane of fur that ringed her neck, and lashed her thick tail, armored scutes clashing and scraping the stone. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">\u201cYour tastes always ran toward the monstrous, Inyonyi. What is that, a new chimera? You weren\u2019t satisfied being a wolf-goat? Now you\u2019re some kind of crocodile-lion. It is not met,\u201d Alafia said with a confrontational laugh.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Her massive jaws did not move as Inyonyi spoke. \u201cWe are all of us authors of identity, Alafia. Some of us claim monstrous ones. A few of us are even honest about it.\u201d</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Alafia snarled, and the locks of her hair came alive, whipping back and forth as if caught in some unearthly gale, twisting into braids, and each braid bore a little sting, like the one that slept beneath the skin of her right arm. The pearl in her throat throbbed and swelled to the size of an apple, a hard knot at her collarbone, red light spilling from behind her clenched teeth.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">\u201cAh,\u201d rumbled Inyonyi, \u201cyour burning necklace. Do I anger you, Prince of the Earth? Do you see fit to vomit burning venom upon me, to render me to guts and ash? It is not met,\u201d she said.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">\u201cif drinking is bitter,\u201d sing-songed a lumpen little goblin, trapped under a shard of marble--</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">\u201cbecome wine.\u201d </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">A moment passed. Alafia did not vomit burning venom, nor did she become wine, though drinking was bitter-- so bitter, bitterer than time and ruin and sadness. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">\u201cNo,\u201d she said, braids uncurling into human hair again, \u201cI do not see fit. What do you want Inyonyi? Why have you intruded upon my hermitage? To mock my sorrow, and my loss?\u201d</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">A gust of fetid breath, heavy with the smell of rotted meat, blasted from the chimera\u2019s mouth. \u201cSelf-pitying fool! Have you not heard? Are you so consumed with your regrets and your failures that you have come wholly detached from the world and sound? Have you no birds flitting back to you? Have you no spies? No proteges, no insurgencies, no wonderlands?\u201d</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">\u201cWhat are you driving at, Inyonyi?\u201d</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">\u201cThe Empress is vanished and they have returned. Three years ago, Alafia, they began to return. And you, lost in sad reflection.\u201d Inyonyi shook her maned, scaled, fanged head. The great witch-beast, survivor of the Shogunate, drinker of heart\u2019s-blood, turned and began to stalk away.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Alafia stood with mouth agape. They had returned. </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>She </i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">had returned. Had she? After all those years locked away in the cold embrace of death, might there be a flash of gold at last?</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">\u201cWait!\u201d she cried.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Inyonyi did not cease her heavy-footed exit. \u201cYou would ask me for a name. I will not give it to you. Go and see, sorrow-hawk. Go and see.\u201d And with that, the chimera\u2019s form fractured like a broken mirror and dissolved into darkness and screaming wings. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">High above, the moon peeked through a cloud.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Alafia, broken-hearted. Alafia of the Burning Necklace. Alafia, a fallen queen upon a wounded throne. Alafia, a mistress of transformations and prodigy in the night-craft. She had languished for a mortal lifetime in obscurity and self-defeat, but she was a cunning creature and beloved of the gods. The goblins of the place began to flock toward her, skitter-skulking, whispering her name-- and one other. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">It takes only a moment. Transformation only ever does. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">She becomes an instrument of defiance once more.</span></span> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">***</span></span><br /> <br /> I hope you enjoyed it! If you want to throw critiques at it, feel free, I'm trying to get back into the Exalted swing of things! Thanks!<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1201-fitter-happier","name":"Fitter Happier","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1201_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"58"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}